{"call_id":"call_SSpQDbzILjIZTBuQEEC6dwtj","process_id":"36542","turn_id":"019ca30e-d082-7481-81fa-2db019089bad","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task get @01KJDQ14"],"cwd":"/workspace","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task get @01KJDQ14"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"kspec setup should work without CLAUDECODE=1 env var in non-interactive contexts. Either add a --age\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KJDQ142M8AM5HAYQBBG12VRS\nType:      task\nStatus:    pending\nPriority:  3\nAutomation: eligible\n\n─── Description ───\n  **What**: `kspec setup` requires the `CLAUDECODE=1` environment variable (or `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` or `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`) to detect the agent type as `claude-code`. In non-interactive contexts like containerized ralph runners, these env vars may not be available, causing `detectAgent()` to return `unknown` and setup to fail or print manual instructions instead of auto-configuring. **Where**: `src/cli/commands/setup.ts` — the `detectAgent()` function (line 82-100) checks `process.env.CLAUDECODE`, `process.env.CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT`, and `process.env.CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. The `registerSetupCommand()` function (line 1638-1655) has options like `--dry-run`, `--author`, `--no-hooks` etc. but no `--agent` flag. The `getSetupStatus()` function (line 774) and the main setup action (line 1345) both call `detectAgent()`. **How**: Add an `--agent <type>` option to `kspec setup` that explicitly specifies the agent type, bypassing `detectAgent()`. Supported values: `claude-code`, `cline`, `cursor`, `windsurf`, `unknown`. When `--agent` is provided, skip detection and use the provided type directly. Also consider a fallback detection: if env vars are absent, check for `~/.claude` directory existence as a weaker signal for `claude-code`. The option should be threaded through to both `runSetup()` and `getSetupStatus()`. **Done when**: (1) `kspec setup --agent claude-code` works without any CLAUDECODE env var set. (2) `kspec setup --status --agent claude-code` reports correct status. (3) `detectAgent()` still works as before when `--agent` is not provided. (4) Invalid `--agent` values are rejected with a clear error. (5) Tests in `tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts` and `tests/setup-pipeline-unification.test.ts` updated.\nSpec ref:  @enhanced-setup\nCreated:   2026-02-26T19:32:51.412Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nEnhanced Setup Command\nType: feature\nImplementation: implemented\nDescription:\n  Orchestrate full onboarding pipeline in kspec setup: detect agent, install hooks\n  (including all PreToolUse guards), render skills, generate agent instructions,\n  scaffold AGENTS.md. Also ship templates in npm package.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: a project with kspec initialized and skills in meta\n    When: kspec setup is run\n    Then: a summary is displayed listing each step performed\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: kspec setup completes\n    When: .claude/settings.json is inspected\n    Then: all hook entries (UserPromptSubmit, Stop, PreToolUse) are present\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: kspec setup completes with skills in meta\n    When: skill availability is inspected\n    Then: rendered skill files exist for project/local skills targeting claude-code and core skills are available via marketplace registration\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: kspec setup completes\n    When: the project root is inspected\n    Then: kspec-agents.md exists\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: --skip-skills flag is provided\n    When: kspec setup is run\n    Then: skill rendering is skipped\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: --dry-run flag is provided\n    When: kspec setup is run\n    Then: planned actions are displayed without making any changes\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: --status flag is provided\n    When: kspec setup is run\n    Then: current state is reported including agent detected and plugin marketplace status (marketplaceRegistered, marketplaceHealthy, pluginEnabled)\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: --status flag is provided with a broken marketplace path\n    When: output is inspected\n    Then: hooks status, skills rendered count, agents.md freshness, and plugin health (including path-broken detection) are shown\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: kspec setup completes in a project configured for ralph loop mode\n    When: the installed skills are checked\n    Then: skills referenced by ralph prompts (task-work, reflect) are present\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-dry-run ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: command supports dry run\n    When: --dry-run flag is provided\n    Then: show what would be changed without applying\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: command completes\n    Then: no files are modified\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: output is shown\n    Then: clear indication that this is a preview\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run mode is active\n    When: command would error\n    Then: error shown but no state changed\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: --dry-run and --force both provided\n    When: command executes\n    Then: dry run takes precedence (no changes made)\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-dry-run)\n    Given: dry run in JSON mode\n    When: --dry-run --json provided\n    Then: JSON output includes dry_run boolean field\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-error-guidance ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes description of what went wrong\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes suggested action to resolve\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: reference not found\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: invalid state transition\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates current state and vali