-agent claude-code` works without any CLAUDECODE env var set. (2) `kspec setup --status --agent claude-code` reports correct status. (3) `detectAgent()` still works as before when `--agent` is not provided. (4) Invalid `--agent` values are rejected with a clear error. (5) Tests in `tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts` and `tests/setup-pipeline-unification.test.ts` updated.\nSpec ref:  @enhanced-setup\nCreated:   2026-02-26T19:32:51.412Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nEnhanced Setup Command\nType: feature\nImplementation: implemented\nDescription:\n  Orchestrate full onboarding pipeline in kspec setup: detect agent, install hooks\n  (including all PreToolUse guards), render skills, generate agent instructions,\n  scaffold AGENTS.md. Also ship templates in npm package.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: a project with kspec initialized and skills in meta\n    When: kspec setup is run\n    Then: a summary is displayed listing each step performed\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: kspec setup completes\n    When: .claude/settings.json is inspected\n    Then: all hook entries (UserPromptSubmit, Stop, PreToolUse) are present\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: kspec setup completes with skills in meta\n    When: skill availability is inspected\n    Then: rendered skill files exist for project/local skills targeting claude-code and core skills are available via marketplace registration\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: kspec setup completes\n    When: the project root is inspected\n    Then: kspec-agents.md exists\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: --skip-skills flag is provided\n    When: kspec setup is run\n    Then: skill rendering is skipped\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: --dry-run flag is provided\n    When: kspec setup is run\n    Then: planned actions are displayed without making any changes\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: --status flag is provided\n    When: kspec setup is run\n    Then: current state is reported including agent detected and plugin marketplace status (marketplaceRegistered, marketplaceHealthy, pluginEnabled)\n  [ac-8]\n  